    {
      "id": "4bcc13f4-cb8c-4b00-8c5a-5a6029a36631",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -460,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 400,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## Post real estate listing reels to Facebook and Instagram\n\n**Who it's for:** real estate agents and brokerages that keep listings in Airtable and post every new listing to Facebook and Instagram.\n\n**What it does:** when a listing is marked ready, it checks the record, writes a hook and two captions with OpenAI, renders a 15 second branded reel with Orshot, posts it to your Facebook Page and Instagram Reels, and writes the post links back to Airtable. Failures are marked in Airtable and emailed to the agent.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect Airtable, OpenAI, Orshot and Gmail credentials.\n2. Add these Airtable fields: Address, City, Price, Bedrooms, Bathrooms, Square feet, Highlights, Photos (attachments), Agent name, Agent email, Listing URL, Post at, Status, Ready at (last modified time of Status), Video URL, Facebook post, Instagram post, Error.\n3. Create a view called **Ready to post** that shows records where Status is Ready to post.\n4. Copy the reel template into your Orshot workspace and paste its ID into **Render listing reel**.\n5. Connect your Facebook Page and Instagram account in Orshot, then pick them in the two publish nodes.\n\nFull guide: https://orshot.com/blog/automate-real-estate-listings-instagram-facebook"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "26de3034-c4ba-4eda-a454-def2a867525f",
      "name": "Check",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        180,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "### 1. Check the listing\nOnly complete listings move on. Missing address, price or photos are marked **Missing info** with the missing field in Error."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fc8e8554-0bb2-481d-86e1-6efb50a4c540",
      "name": "Captions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        680,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 580,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "### 2. Prepare and write copy\nFormats price and specs, picks up to 5 photos, then OpenAI writes a short hook for the video plus separate Facebook and Instagram captions."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b88d2c90-77d5-493a-b8ca-0cab1581c42e",
      "name": "Render",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1280,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 900,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "### 3. Render and publish\nOrshot renders the reel from your template and waits for the video. If the render fails, nothing is posted. The video is then posted to Facebook and Instagram, each with its own caption. Fill **Post at** in Airtable to schedule instead of posting now."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "aeef6d59-3cef-4d58-b6af-44b7769d76f8",
      "name": "Save",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2200,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1200,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "### 4. Save results and alerts\nBoth post links and the video URL are saved on the record. If rendering or either post fails, the record is marked **Failed** and the agent gets an email with the reason."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
